  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nDry conditions overnight and through the day on Saturday. Patchy fog\nwill be possible this morning generally near and southeast of \nInterstate 71. Saturday is expected to be the warmest day of the week\nwith high temperatures in the middle to upper 80s.  \n\nShowers and thunderstorms will start to work into the area overnight\nSaturday night and moreso into the day on Sunday. Cannot rule out\nsome strong to isolated severe storms on Sunday as a cold front\napproaches and moves through the region. Outside of storms breezy\nconditions will be possible Sunday into Sunday night.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nMuch cooler and drier conditions will be in place for Monday with\nhigh temperatures only in the low to middle 70s. Storm chances work\nback into the forecast at times for Tuesday through Friday morning.\nWednesday night into Thursday morning has the highest chance for more\nwidespread shower and thunderstorm activity. Breezy conditions will \nalso be present for Wednesday and Thursday as well.",
